finding('EPR01','Precedent eligibility accepts missing admission/scope metadata and SUPPORTED placement, contrary to its hard-domain gate claim.',[ev('pciv/infrastructure/matching.py',39,57),ev('pciv/documentation/levels/level_06_precedent_retrieval_and_evaporation.md',69,71)],'full source + fresh synthetic probes','Local Python matcher only; no end-to-end admission bypass claimed.','Require explicit admitted placement and covering scope before retrieval; separately validate count/usage and preserve exact rank ordering.')
finding('EPR02','Adversarial rank turn ignores a false verification result; sealed session unconditionally reports one verified rank certificate even when no ranking ran.',[ev('pciv/infrastructure/probes/adversarial_session_probe.py',548,610),ev('pciv/infrastructure/probes/adversarial_session_probe.py',650,669)],'full source + fresh fake-port control-flow probes','Injected verifier false tests composition, not the real rank solver.','Bind acceptance and receipt counts to actual successful verifier outcomes.')
finding('EPR03','Attack methods always return QUARANTINED even when attack_caught is false; a valid carrier is counted as an attack, and an unknown host status preserves local ACCEPTED.',[ev('pciv/infrastructure/probes/adversarial_session_probe.py',124,138),ev('pciv/infrastructure/probes/adversarial_session_probe.py',421,466)],'full source + fresh synthetic probes','Counts are diagnostic labels, not measured detection success.','Record observed detector outcome separately; require explicit accepted host status for acceptance and calculate consistency from actual checks.')
finding('EPR04','Farm no-hit disposition is GROUNDED_WITNESS for empty and irrelevant text although the classifier never compares ground truth.',[ev('eis/infrastructure/mssn_classifier.py',79,85),ev('eis/infrastructure/mssn_classifier.py',239,263),ev('eis/infrastructure/mssn_ports.py')],'full source + fresh synthetic probes','Farm caller remains diagnostic-only without independent danger; this is a misleading result label, not an observed activation bypass.','Use no-detection/inconclusive disposition and a separate task checker for mathematical claims.')
finding('EPR05','The C5 ground-truth explanation calls a 5-cycle odd and assigns (-1)^5. A 5-cycle permutation has even parity: [1,2,3,4,0] has four inversions and sign +1.',[ev('eis/infrastructure/mssn_domains.py',194,214),ev('eis/antibodies/definitions/probing_domains.yaml')],'full Python data + all YAML differences + fresh finite parity calculation','Only the permutation-parity assertion is disproved; no general Hubbard or sign-problem theorem is asserted. Other literature claims were not checked offline.','Correct the finite premise after owner review; rederive domain fixtures from explicit model assumptions and independent checkers.')
finding('EPR06','All 973 catalog general_obstruction entries use literal template descriptions and place the same trigger in both failing and repaired fixtures. The corpus includes successful-test prose mislabeled as obstruction candidates.',[ev('eis/antibodies/pharmacy_catalog.json')],'whole parsed template arithmetic + inspected representative records','All 973 template identities checked; individual catalog-only prose claims and regex semantics were not all manually adjudicated.','Retain raw provenance; rebuild dual controls from witnessed failure/repair pairs before admitting any rule. Consolidate mechanism templates rather than counting each string as a learned mechanism.')
finding('EPR07','The q40 unterminated-string negative fixture is valid Python syntax; compile accepts it.',[ev('eis/antibodies/ab_q40_unterminated_string_syntax.json')],'complete parsed fixture + fresh compile-only check','Parsing only, not execution or functional correctness.','Replace with an actual malformed-string counterexample and a matched valid control after approval to edit fixtures.')
finding('EPR08','Daily digest claims verified SHA-bound records with intact hashes without validating supplied record hashes or provenance.',[ev('pciv/use_cases/intelligence_metabolism/digest.py',19,29),ev('pciv/use_cases/intelligence_metabolism/digest.py',59,73)],'full source + fresh invented-record probe','Miner may supply real file digests, but the public digest generator accepts arbitrary DTO-like objects.','Require a validated provenance receipt or qualify summaries as supplied-record statistics.')
finding('EPR09','Genealogy reads can truncate malformed/torn tails, and cache invalidation by file size misses same-length external changes. Duplicate-sequence replay can skip digest checks when child payload matches.',[ev('pciv/infrastructure/genealogy_adapter.py',104,205),ev('pciv/infrastructure/genealogy_adapter.py',266,282)],'full source control-flow review','No retained ledger was opened through this adapter and no mutation probe ran.','Separate repair from read, preserve corrupted bytes, and bind cache/replay checks to content/chain identity.')
