finding('EPR11','The population notebook allocates cap 10 as [6,2,2] while Level 07 requires [6,3,1]; reverse tuple sorting gives the tie to Baseline instead of Unmeasured.',[ev('pciv/documentation/curriculum/420_population_reserves_persistence/notebooks/lesson_420_07_ecological_reserves_and_population.ipynb'),ev('pciv/documentation/levels/level_07_ecological_reserves_and_population.md',77,87)],'all notebook cells/outputs inspected + fresh extracted-function probe','No notebook execution history exists; this demonstrates the toy helper, not the production allocator.','Use exact integer remainders and declared tie order, then compare notebook against canonical owner.')
finding('EPR12','Other notebooks advertise broader verification than their predicates: one damped sum is not PageRank, one payload hash is not crash replay, and scalar attenuation does not traverse a genealogy.',[ev('pciv/documentation/curriculum/410_selection_ranking_retrieval/notebooks/lesson_410_05_inverse_lineage_pagerank.ipynb'),ev('pciv/documentation/curriculum/420_population_reserves_persistence/notebooks/lesson_420_09_durable_event_log_and_persistence.ipynb'),ev('pciv/documentation/curriculum/400_prompt_civ_foundations/notebooks/lesson_400_03_lamarckian_retro_inheritance.ipynb')],'all retained notebook cells/outputs inspected','Eleven notebooks retain no executed cell counts or outputs. Illustrations can be useful without certifying production behavior.','Label illustrations accurately and use canonical owner tests for execution claims.')
finding('EPR13','In the boundary-repair validation artifact, 21 of 33 output_utf8/output_sha256 pairs disagree under exact UTF-8 hashing of the retained string.',[ev('eis/receipts/epic_boundary_repair_20261012/validation.json')],'whole-artifact automated hash recomputation','This identifies byte-binding inconsistency, not fabrication; relocation, normalization or postprocessing may explain it. Historical commands were not rerun.','Preserve the receipt, locate original raw logs/normalization provenance, and do not treat the embedded text as hash-verified output until reconciled.')
finding('EPR14','Catalog has 29 admitted labels but only two embedded admission records; the repaired Pilot 035 pair explicitly supersedes older finite-to-unrestricted claim patterns.',[ev('eis/antibodies/pharmacy_catalog.json'),ev('eis/antibodies/definitions/pilot035_candidates.json'),ev('eis/antibodies/admissions/pilot035_owner_approval_20261015.json')],'whole parsed status inventory + complete parsed candidate/approval records','A missing embedded record does not prove no external authorization exists; legacy status alone is insufficient evidence of authenticated activation.','Consolidate through the explicit admission owner and exact scope; keep historical domain answers out of new workflow inputs.')
finding('EPR15','Mined antiskill set contains 22 entries but 18 unique candidate IDs. Root/spec YAML copies also diverge in old import paths, native binding paths and one harmful-control test name.',[ev('eis/antiskills/ooutwire/evidence_mined_candidates.json'),ev('eis/antibodies/specs/anti_witness_certificate_desynchronization.yaml'),ev('eis/antibodies/specs/anti_implicit_credential_discovery.yaml')],'all candidate invariants + whole schema duplicate inventory + complete YAML field differences','Duplication is not a reason to delete historical evidence; no semantic theorem validated by byte equality.','Choose one authoritative definition with migration aliases; remove duplicate candidate counting only after provenance-preserving review.')
finding('EPR16','Some anti-theorem fixtures still encode assumed answers: scalar-proxy repair returns hardcoded truth/negative-value fields, while target-fitting repair computes a sum in a field named 2S-minus-2P.',[ev('eis/antibodies/anti_scalar_proxy_theorem_substitution.yaml'),ev('eis/antibodies/anti_target_fitting_constant_compensation.yaml')],'complete parsed fixture bodies inspected','These are lexical examples, not independent PSD or atomic-physics verification. The arithmetic label mismatch is local; physical constants were not adjudicated.','Use explicit matrix/vector or independently pinned subchannel inputs and recompute the actual obligation; keep lexical examples diagnostic.')

finding('EPR17','The EIS cross-context architecture helper recognizes only roots starting with engine; pciv, pfp, operads and operations imports are invisible to that predicate.',[ev('eis/tests/architecture/test_clean_architecture_ast_boundaries.py',92,109),ev('eis/tests/architecture/test_clean_architecture_ast_boundaries.py',123,144)],'full test body + one fresh pure extracted-helper probe','This demonstrates an underinclusive test predicate, not an actual forbidden production import or a failing full architecture suite.','Declare the canonical context roots and add representative renamed-root countercontrols before using this test as a cross-context coverage claim.')
finding('EPR18','Two test files exercise a locally defined helper rather than the production operation: challenger decay and promoted-operand filtering.',[ev('eis/tests/unit/test_challenger_adversarial_stress.py',716,740),ev('pciv/tests/intelligence_metabolism/test_operand_registry.py',12,58)],'full test-body source review','Local formula/filter examples can be useful; their passing would not constrain a separately implemented production path. No test was executed.','Keep pedagogical examples labeled as such and bind production regression claims to the owning production function and adversarial controls.')
finding('EPR19','The qualification lifecycle test supplies closure.verified=True; the asserted DISCHARGED result does not independently verify the named formal qualification.',[ev('eis/tests/unit/test_qualification_ab_limit_honesty.py',117,219)],'full fixture and assertion review','This is a premise-bound lifecycle transition test. The native kernel and actual qualification owner were not run here.','Separate evidence validation from lifecycle transitions and require a bound executed checker result before claiming the open obligation has been discharged.')
finding('EPR20','Run U manually rewrites pharmacy_status to admitted before its antibody-blocking bout; the legacy file-store test similarly edits status to ACTIVE.',[ev('pciv/tests/integration/test_run_u_cemetery_blocking_loop.py',236,295),ev('pciv/tests/unit/test_cemetery_and_genealogy.py',71,88)],'full test fixture/control-flow review','Finite blocking after supplied admission is not autonomous activation from harvested failures, and this is not a newly observed production bypass.','Describe the admission premise explicitly and keep authentication/admission-owner tests separate from downstream blocking tests.')
finding('EPR21','Level 00 excludes protected_spans from the genome identity tuple, while the current ecology test requires span changes to change prompt_id.',[ev('pciv/documentation/levels/level_00_substrate_and_packaging.md',61,73),ev('pciv/tests/unit/test_prompt_ecology.py',121,134)],'full prose and full test-body comparison','Documentation/test contract mismatch; no fresh canonical identity implementation run. SHA collision resistance is also an assumption, not an injectivity theorem.','Reconcile the documented identity envelope with its canonical owner, and distinguish derived metadata from identity-bound protected spans.')
finding('EPR22','Level 07 declares reserve fractions 3/5, 1/4, 3/20, yielding 12/5/3 at cap 20, while the unit test expects 12/6/2.',[ev('pciv/documentation/levels/level_07_ecological_reserves_and_population.md',71,89),ev('pciv/tests/unit/test_backfill_and_coverage_gates.py',643,656),ev('pciv/tests/unit/test_prompt_ecology.py',137,145)],'full prose/test comparison + direct exact arithmetic','Cap 10 happens to agree at 6/3/1. This is a policy inconsistency between artifacts, not a fresh allocator test or claim of optimal fractions.','Choose and version the actual quota policy; compare every curriculum and test vector at noncoincident caps before claiming parity.')
finding('EPR23','Short lessons diverge from their fuller mathematical contracts: inverse rank says power iteration with duality-gap termination instead of Gaussian elimination, and retrieval decay omits floor(t/H).',[ev('pciv/documentation/curriculum/410_selection_ranking_retrieval/concepts/lesson_410_05_inverse_lineage_pagerank.md',20,26),ev('pciv/documentation/levels/level_05_inverse_lineage_pagerank.md',73,86),ev('pciv/documentation/curriculum/410_selection_ranking_retrieval/concepts/lesson_410_06_precedent_retrieval_and_evaporation.md',20,26),ev('pciv/documentation/levels/level_06_precedent_retrieval_and_evaporation.md',82,87)],'complete prose-body comparison','These are different algorithms/decay policies, not harmless formatting differences. No convergence theorem or biological analogy was established here.','Align lesson equations and algorithm names with a pinned canonical implementation and preserve their finite assumptions.')
finding('EPR24','The Level 02 half-open overlap formula does not cover zero-width insertion, although its later invariant and production fixture explicitly require refusing insertion inside a protected span.',[ev('pciv/documentation/levels/level_02_mutation_operators_and_forge.md',66,72),ev('pciv/documentation/levels/level_02_mutation_operators_and_forge.md',109,113),ev('pciv/tests/unit/test_backfill_and_coverage_gates.py',622,630)],'full prose/test comparison + empty-interval reasoning','For len=0 the edit interval is empty, so nonempty-intersection alone cannot enforce insertion protection. This is a specification gap, not a claim the production forge permits it.','Specify insertion-point containment separately from positive-width overlap and retain the zero-width regression control.')

